# Database Setup

This project uses Supabase as the backend.

## Required Environment Variables

Create a `.env.local` file with:

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

---

## Required Tables

The app expects these tables:

- resume_versions
- job_applications
- folders
- cover_letters

---

## Required Columns (resume_versions)

The following columns must exist:

- id
- name
- resume_text
- profile_image
- company_logo
- contact_info
- accent_color
- job_description
- folder_id
- profile_photo_border
- target_box_bg_color
- target_box_border_color
- created_at
- updated_at

---

## Important Notes

- The database schema must match `lib/storage.ts`
- If columns are missing, saving will fail with runtime errors
- Add new columns via SQL scripts in `/scripts`
- Do NOT rely on manual fixes in Supabase only — always record changes

---

## Known Migration

Run this SQL if resume saving fails:

```sql
alter table resume_versions
add column if not exists profile_photo_border boolean default true;

alter table resume_versions
add column if not exists target_box_bg_color text;

alter table resume_versions
add column if not exists target_box_border_color text;